1587
00:55:04,800 --> 00:55:07,200
She's just like all the rest,
you'll see.

1588
00:55:07,233 --> 00:55:08,933
Lay down, pop.

1589
00:55:08,967 --> 00:55:10,267
I'll be right back.

1590
00:55:10,300 --> 00:55:12,600
SERVO: Just stay there
and hallucinate.

1591
00:55:12,633 --> 00:55:16,100
MIKE: Oh, not on our
one piece of furniture.

1592
00:55:16,133 --> 00:55:18,000
-Marv...
-SERVO: Ugh.

1593
00:55:18,033 --> 00:55:19,067
...don't go.

1594
00:55:20,067 --> 00:55:23,667
You're my son, you're all
I got left in the world.

1595
00:55:23,700 --> 00:55:25,833
CROW: Besides my lucky table.

1596
00:55:28,700 --> 00:55:29,833
MIKE: You know, the thing is,

1597
00:55:29,867 --> 00:55:31,533
he isn't even close
to hitting bottom.

1598
00:55:31,567 --> 00:55:32,600
-SERVO: Mm-mmm.
-Come on, pop.

1599
00:55:32,633 --> 00:55:34,333
I'll help you on the sofa.

1600
00:55:35,300 --> 00:55:37,667
SERVO: Come on.
Let's change that diaper.

1601
00:55:39,767 --> 00:55:40,733
CROW: Dad, come on.

1602
00:55:40,767 --> 00:55:42,367
We've got our Webelos meeting.

1603
00:55:42,400 --> 00:55:43,867
See you right back, pop.

1604
00:55:45,433 --> 00:55:46,400
When I get back,

1605
00:55:47,400 --> 00:55:50,033
maybe we can show them all
a thing or two.

1606
00:55:50,067 --> 00:55:51,433
SERVO: Pop? Pop.

1607
00:55:51,467 --> 00:55:52,733
Pop. Oh, my God.

1608
00:55:52,767 --> 00:55:54,000
Come on, pop. Live.

1609
00:55:54,033 --> 00:55:55,333
Damn it. Live.

1610
00:55:56,767 --> 00:55:58,733
MIKE: Hand me the remote, son.

1611
00:56:00,567 --> 00:56:01,900
[ Music playing ]

1612
00:56:01,933 --> 00:56:04,033
SERVO: Meanwhile,
Betty, earns some extra credit

1613
00:56:04,067 --> 00:56:05,167
after school.

1614
00:56:06,100 --> 00:56:08,467
CROW: Van Cliburn
entertains a groupie.

1615
00:56:10,467 --> 00:56:12,267
Boy, if the class
could see me now.

1616
00:56:12,300 --> 00:56:13,500
CROW: We can!

1617
00:56:13,533 --> 00:56:15,800
They'd just be jealous,
that's all.

1618
00:56:15,833 --> 00:56:17,700
-Honey, I don't know if...
-MIKE: My hands are stuck

1619
00:56:17,733 --> 00:56:19,667
-to your head.
-Well, you know,

1620
00:56:19,700 --> 00:56:21,833
I'm supposed to be so hard

1621
00:56:21,867 --> 00:56:24,233
and tough and all.

1622
00:56:24,267 --> 00:56:25,767
Tell me you love me.

1623
00:56:25,800 --> 00:56:27,200
SERVO: You love me.

1624
00:56:28,800 --> 00:56:30,600
I love you.

1625
00:56:30,633 --> 00:56:31,633
Again.

1626
00:56:31,667 --> 00:56:33,567
CROW: I can't hear you, worm.

1627
00:56:33,600 --> 00:56:35,733
I love you, baby.

1628
00:56:35,767 --> 00:56:36,967
I love you.

1629
00:56:37,000 --> 00:56:38,233
When are you gonna prove it?

1630
00:56:38,267 --> 00:56:40,467
MIKE: Oh,
should I give you a deposition?

1631
00:56:40,500 --> 00:56:41,633
Prove it?

1632
00:56:42,500 --> 00:56:44,700
You mean, you don't believe me?

1633
00:56:44,733 --> 00:56:46,100
Oh, I believe it.

1634
00:56:47,200 --> 00:56:50,400
But a girl likes to see
something real, you know.

1635
00:56:50,433 --> 00:56:51,867
SERVO:
Something in a mutual fund.

1636
00:56:51,900 --> 00:56:54,233
What do you mean?
Like a car or jewels

1637
00:56:54,267 --> 00:56:55,900
or something?

1638
00:56:55,933 --> 00:56:57,500
Oh, or something.

1639
00:56:57,533 --> 00:57:00,633
CROW: Like a supersoaker
in a nudie suit.

1640
00:57:00,667 --> 00:57:02,733
You'll have it all
someday, baby.

1641
00:57:03,900 --> 00:57:05,600
I swear it, you'll have it all.

1642
00:57:05,633 --> 00:57:07,000
When?

1643
00:57:07,033 --> 00:57:08,500
-Soon.
-CROW: How's Thursday?

1644
00:57:08,533 --> 00:57:10,400
When I got out of school
and have a chance

1645
00:57:10,433 --> 00:57:11,467
to look around a little.

1646
00:57:11,500 --> 00:57:12,833
SERVO:
Inventing the desktop computer.

1647
00:57:12,867 --> 00:57:14,467
Now, what if someone comes along

1648
00:57:14,500 --> 00:57:16,333
