1649
00:57:16,967 --> 00:57:19,033
CROW: Stuff and stuff.

1650
00:57:19,067 --> 00:57:20,900
I'd kill him and take it away.

1651
00:57:20,933 --> 00:57:22,267
SERVO:
That is correct. Let's move on

1652
00:57:22,300 --> 00:57:23,567
to the lightning round.

1653
00:57:23,600 --> 00:57:25,600
Tell me again.

1654
00:57:25,633 --> 00:57:27,400
SERVO: I forgot what I said.

1655
00:57:27,433 --> 00:57:29,067
I love you, baby.

1656
00:57:29,833 --> 00:57:32,000
CROW: There's that Vince magic.

1657
00:57:33,167 --> 00:57:34,833
SERVO: He's gonna bowl
his troubles away.

1658
00:57:34,867 --> 00:57:37,400
MIKE: The mean streets
of Appleton.

1659
00:57:37,433 --> 00:57:40,133
Hey, I'm fake-walking here.

1660
00:57:40,167 --> 00:57:43,167
[ Music playing ]

1661
00:57:44,867 --> 00:57:47,300
CROW: He's surveying
his liquor kingdom.

1662
00:57:47,333 --> 00:57:48,700
It's Gigot.

1663
00:57:49,633 --> 00:57:51,200
I think the point-
of-purchase displays

1664
00:57:51,233 --> 00:57:53,100
have gotten
a little out of hand.

1665
00:57:53,133 --> 00:57:54,300
SERVO:
Where's the bread display?

1666
00:57:54,333 --> 00:57:57,367
[ Music playing ]

1667
00:57:57,400 --> 00:57:58,800
MIKE:
Here's one of the great one's

1668
00:57:58,833 --> 00:58:00,167
classic routines.

1669
00:58:00,200 --> 00:58:01,467
CROW: [ Laughs ]

1670
00:58:01,500 --> 00:58:03,700
It's the all impulse item store.

1671
00:58:03,733 --> 00:58:06,300
[ Music playing ]

1672
00:58:06,333 --> 00:58:08,200
SERVO: It's nutty, huh.

1673
00:58:08,233 --> 00:58:10,533
MIKE: Tonight,
on Lou Jacobi Playhouse.

1674
00:58:10,567 --> 00:58:13,433
[ Music playing ]

1675
00:58:13,467 --> 00:58:16,467
CROW: Ooh, that's good booze.

1676
00:58:18,833 --> 00:58:20,267
SERVO: And now back to our show.

1677
00:58:20,300 --> 00:58:21,833
Get your mitts
out of my register.

1678
00:58:21,867 --> 00:58:24,567
Samuel, please, my most
valuable possessions.

1679
00:58:24,600 --> 00:58:27,267
Sure, for stealing my cigars,
drinking my wine,

1680
00:58:27,300 --> 00:58:29,033
and dipping
into my cash register.

1681
00:58:29,067 --> 00:58:31,733
Samuel, I'm shocked.
Your own flesh and blood.

1682
00:58:31,767 --> 00:58:33,300
SERVO: Mostly flesh.

1683
00:58:33,333 --> 00:58:34,500
My what?

1684
00:58:34,533 --> 00:58:36,067
Just because
I'm married to your sister

1685
00:58:36,100 --> 00:58:37,700
doesn't give you
cause to come in

1686
00:58:37,733 --> 00:58:39,533
and nail my inventory.

1687
00:58:39,567 --> 00:58:40,767
Well, she's your wife,
isn't she?

1688
00:58:40,800 --> 00:58:42,500
-Yeah, but...
-And she's my sister.

1689
00:58:42,533 --> 00:58:43,367
-Sure.
-Then you admit it,

1690
00:58:43,400 --> 00:58:44,767
what yours is mine.

1691
00:58:44,800 --> 00:58:46,300
CROW:
I like this new movie better.

1692
00:58:46,333 --> 00:58:48,100
Look, I don't wanna be a nag.

1693
00:58:48,133 --> 00:58:50,033
Why don't you go get a job?

1694
00:58:50,067 --> 00:58:53,300
A job? Would you have
a doctor take up a pick?

1695
00:58:53,333 --> 00:58:56,233
A chemist sit
behind the wheel of a truck?

1696
00:58:56,267 --> 00:58:58,867
If he was making a bum
out of me, I would.

1697
00:58:58,900 --> 00:59:00,933
Samuel, I'm a professional man.

1698
00:59:00,967 --> 00:59:02,267
There's no other way.

1699
00:59:02,300 --> 00:59:04,233
Now, you were in the rackets,
you ought to know that.

1700
00:59:04,267 --> 00:59:06,267
Yeah, but I gave it up
10 years ago.

1701
00:59:06,300 --> 00:59:08,033
[ Phone ringing ]

1702
00:59:08,067 --> 00:59:09,867
CROW: I hope that's
the scene police calling.

1703
00:59:09,900 --> 00:59:10,900
SAMUEL: Sam's.

1704
00:59:10,933 --> 00:59:12,267
Hello?

1705
00:59:12,300 --> 00:59:13,333
Yeah.

1706
00:59:13,367 --> 00:59:14,500
Yeah, dear.

1707
00:59:14,533 --> 00:59:16,600
-Potatoes?
-SERVO: Potatoes, tomatoes,

1708
00:59:16,633 --> 00:59:17,467
-tomatoes?
-Bread?

1709
00:59:17,500 --> 00:59:19,000
Yeah, I'll pick it up.

1710
00:59:19,033 --> 00:59:20,700
No, I won't forget.

1711
00:59:20,733 --> 00:59:22,400
Yeah, good bye, dear.
I'll talk to you later.

1712
00:59:22,433 --> 00:59:23,300
Bye-bye.

1713
00:59:23,333 --> 00:59:25,033
CROW: Damn Jerky Boys.

1714
00:59:25,067 --> 00:59:27,133
Your sister.

1715
00:59:27,167 --> 00:59:28,667
Your wife.

1716
00:59:28,700 --> 00:59:32,500
Samuel, you are the last
of the great gentlemen.

1717
00:59:32,533 --> 00:59:33,933
Have a cigar.

1718
00:59:33,967 --> 00:59:36,067
SERVO: Early Edmonds and
Curly isn't that good.

1719
00:59:38,133 --> 00:59:39,700
MIKE: Real nice art direction.

1720
00:59:39,733 --> 00:59:41,233
CROW: Mm-hmm, you can't
art direct those stains

1721
00:59:41,267 --> 00:59:42,600
on the wall.

1722
00:59:42,633 --> 00:59:44,867
Hit it, punk.
You ain't old enough.

1723
00:59:44,900 --> 00:59:46,600
I'm not here to buy liquor.

1724
00:59:46,633 --> 00:59:48,467
Sorry, we're fresh out of Cokes.

1725
00:59:48,500 --> 00:59:50,200
Are you Sam Tolman?

1726
00:59:50,233 --> 00:59:51,200
Yeah. So?

1727
00:59:51,233 --> 00:59:52,900
SERVO: I need a bottle adapter
for my lips.

1728
00:59:52,933 --> 00:59:54,433
I understand you're a friend
of Harry March.

1729
00:59:54,467 --> 00:59:55,700
Harry March?

1730
00:59:55,733 --> 00:59:56,700
Who's Harry March?

1731
00:59:56,733 --> 00:59:58,400
MIKE: Am I in the right movie?

1732
00:59:58,433 --> 01:00:00,200
The best safe cracker around,

1733
01:00:00,233 --> 01:00:02,533
maybe the best in the business.

1734
01:00:02,567 --> 01:00:03,500
Never heard of him.

1735
01:00:04,667 --> 01:00:07,833
Okay. I just thought you might
be interested in a deal.

1736
01:00:07,867 --> 01:00:09,000
Wait a minute, kid.

1737
01:00:09,033 --> 01:00:12,000
-CROW: Is that your real face?
-What kind of a deal?

1738
01:00:12,033 --> 01:00:13,667
What difference does it make?

1739
01:00:13,700 --> 01:00:15,400
You said you didn't know him.

1740
01:00:15,433 --> 01:00:18,300
I make friends real easy.
What kind of a deal?

1741
01:00:18,333 --> 01:00:19,967
MIKE: I haven't figured
that part out yet.

1742
01:00:20,000 --> 01:00:21,033
A big deal.

1743
01:00:21,067 --> 01:00:22,467
CROW: Oh, I'm in.

1744
01:00:22,500 --> 01:00:24,533
A million dollars cash.

1745
01:00:24,567 --> 01:00:26,700
A million dollars cash?

1746
01:00:28,133 --> 01:00:30,433
Kid, I'm busy, why don't
you go tell your fairy tales

1747
01:00:30,467 --> 01:00:33,300
-someplace else?
-I mean it, a million cash.

1748
01:00:33,333 --> 01:00:35,200
And so where is it?
Maybe it's in the Mint

1749
01:00:35,233 --> 01:00:36,367
or maybe it's in Fort Knox?

1750
01:00:36,400 --> 01:00:38,800
It's about six blocks from here.

1751
01:00:38,833 --> 01:00:40,333
You're lying.

1752
01:00:40,367 --> 01:00:43,067
Look, I know where the money is
and I know how to get it.

1753
01:00:43,100 --> 01:00:45,633
All I need is someone
that could open a safe.

1754
01:00:45,667 --> 01:00:46,767
So you ain't lying?

1755
01:00:46,800 --> 01:00:49,200
How does a punk like you
know where a million dollars is?

1756
01:00:49,233 --> 01:00:52,167
SERVO:
I, sir, am a shipping clerk.

1757
01:00:52,200 --> 01:00:54,067
Mr. Tolman, all my life,

1758
01:00:54,100 --> 01:00:55,833
my brains have been
sort of a curse.

1759
01:00:55,867 --> 01:00:57,533
CROW: Unlike Dick Cavett.

1760
01:00:57,567 --> 01:01:00,667
Now, maybe I can make
it pay off for everybody.

1761
01:01:00,700 --> 01:01:02,233
MIKE: Hmm,
chin needs a quick cleaning.

