01:19:23,400 --> 01:19:25,633
[ Music playing ]

2257
01:19:25,667 --> 01:19:26,833
Okay, let's go.

2258
01:19:26,867 --> 01:19:28,433
CROW: Barney,
bring the van around.

2259
01:19:30,500 --> 01:19:32,033
SERVO:
Did everyone make a potty?

2260
01:19:33,200 --> 01:19:34,333
Good luck.

2261
01:19:35,933 --> 01:19:38,267
CROW: So, who's got the car?

2262
01:19:41,933 --> 01:19:44,967
SERVO: Yeah, it takes 11 minutes
if he goes 600 miles an hour.

2263
01:19:45,000 --> 01:19:46,833
CROW: Well, at least
the traffic is with him.

2264
01:19:46,867 --> 01:19:50,167
[ Music playing ]

2265
01:19:50,200 --> 01:19:51,300
SERVO: Almost there yet?

2266
01:19:51,333 --> 01:19:52,767
When are we gonna be there?

2267
01:19:52,800 --> 01:19:53,833
I'm hungry.

2268
01:19:53,867 --> 01:19:55,567
[ Music playing ]

2269
01:19:55,600 --> 01:19:57,033
SERVO:
Marv called everyone in town

2270
01:19:57,067 --> 01:19:58,567
and asked them to stay home.

2271
01:19:58,600 --> 01:20:01,600
[ Music playing ]

2272
01:20:04,733 --> 01:20:06,733
SERVO: I have a test tomorrow,
what am I doing?

2273
01:20:07,800 --> 01:20:10,800
[ Music playing ]

2274
01:20:11,933 --> 01:20:13,467
It's almost 10:51.

2275
01:20:13,500 --> 01:20:14,633
CROW: Oh, we're missing Leno.

2276
01:20:14,667 --> 01:20:16,267
Relax, we'll make it.

2277
01:20:19,133 --> 01:20:22,433
SERVO: So, when does
the suspense part begin?

2278
01:20:22,467 --> 01:20:24,167
[ Music playing ]

2279
01:20:24,200 --> 01:20:27,567
SERVO: So, are your dads
bean-eating alcoholics, too?

2280
01:20:27,600 --> 01:20:29,733
CROW: Marvin should really be
in his car seat.

2281
01:20:31,333 --> 01:20:32,233
SERVO: Oh, no.

2282
01:20:32,267 --> 01:20:34,733
I've seen
this random car directing.

2283
01:20:36,467 --> 01:20:37,633
What is it?

2284
01:20:37,667 --> 01:20:39,100
Looks like an accident.

2285
01:20:39,133 --> 01:20:40,367
What do we do?

2286
01:20:40,400 --> 01:20:42,633
It's the only direct street
to the ferry.

2287
01:20:42,667 --> 01:20:44,033
We'll have to detour.

2288
01:20:44,067 --> 01:20:45,067
Hurry up.

2289
01:20:46,000 --> 01:20:47,167
MIKE: Oh, he is smart.

2290
01:20:47,200 --> 01:20:49,033
That hurry-up part
was pure genius.

2291
01:20:49,067 --> 01:20:50,133
CROW: You bet.

2292
01:20:51,067 --> 01:20:52,167
Oh, sure.

2293
01:20:52,200 --> 01:20:54,333
Let's just sit around the table
and not leave early.

2294
01:20:54,367 --> 01:20:55,800
Good one, Marv.

2295
01:20:56,600 --> 01:20:59,600
[ Tom makes noises ]

2296
01:21:03,533 --> 01:21:04,433
We're there.

2297
01:21:04,467 --> 01:21:05,433
SERVO: It's really important
that,

2298
01:21:05,467 --> 01:21:06,700
♪ Whatever you do ♪

2299
01:21:06,733 --> 01:21:08,300
♪ Don't pay the ferryman ♪

2300
01:21:08,333 --> 01:21:09,833
CROW: Oh, could you do
something about that?

2301
01:21:09,867 --> 01:21:11,033
-MIKE: Okay...
-There's another ferry

2302
01:21:11,067 --> 01:21:11,967
in two minutes.

2303
01:21:12,000 --> 01:21:14,567
SERVO:
♪ Don't even fix a price ♪

2304
01:21:14,600 --> 01:21:16,000
All we do is wait.

2305
01:21:16,800 --> 01:21:18,100
And pray.

2306
01:21:18,133 --> 01:21:20,167
SERVO: Yeah, I'm sure,
what, with wars and famine

2307
01:21:20,200 --> 01:21:21,967
God is really interested
in your heist.

2308
01:21:23,000 --> 01:21:24,833
♪ Until he gets
you to the other side ♪

2309
01:21:24,867 --> 01:21:26,500
MIKE: Okay, that's it.
That's it.

2310
01:21:26,533 --> 01:21:28,100
-Bye-bye.
-CROW: Woo-ho-ho.

2311
01:21:28,133 --> 01:21:29,733
-Yay.
-What time is it?

2312
01:21:30,733 --> 01:21:32,167
-It's 10:58.
-We'll never make it.

2313
01:21:32,200 --> 01:21:33,567
MIKE: It was
a little harsh but...

2314
01:21:33,600 --> 01:21:35,100
-We've got to.
-CROW: It had to be done.

2315
01:21:35,133 --> 01:21:35,700
Come on.

2316
01:21:37,000 --> 01:21:40,000
CROW: Hey, the other side looks
exactly like the other side.

2317
01:21:41,800 --> 01:21:44,833
[ Music playing ]

2318
01:21:44,867 --> 01:21:46,300
MIKE: So does
this heist count towards

2319
01:21:46,333 --> 01:21:48,167
his outcome-based education?

2320
01:21:48,200 --> 01:21:49,533
CROW: Hmm, yes.

2321
01:21:50,733 --> 01:21:51,833
Kill your lights.

2322
01:21:51,867 --> 01:21:53,900
CROW: No, they don't need them
now that it's the middle

2323
01:21:53,933 --> 01:21:55,333
of the afternoon.

2324
01:21:58,133 --> 01:22:01,200
[ Music playing ]

2325
01:22:04,533 --> 01:22:06,133
SERVO: Look at this one.

2326
01:22:07,233 --> 01:22:09,500
CROW: I hope they didn't miss
the film's climax.

2327
01:22:11,267 --> 01:22:13,433
MIKE: I brought
my baritone sax.

2328
01:22:13,467 --> 01:22:14,900
It's almost 11:04.

2329
01:22:14,933 --> 01:22:16,167
We may have missed them.

2330
01:22:16,200 --> 01:22:17,833
SERVO: Again, maybe we didn't.

2331
01:22:17,867 --> 01:22:19,267
Come on.

2332
01:22:21,133 --> 01:22:22,700
CROW:
Oh, it's a sleepover caper.

2333
01:22:22,733 --> 01:22:24,267
[ Giggles ]

2334
01:22:25,267 --> 01:22:27,867
CROW: What's with the Tom
and Jerry music?

2335
01:22:29,233 --> 01:22:31,300
We're never late,
especially tonight.

2336
01:22:31,333 --> 01:22:32,567
What do we do now?

2337
01:22:34,467 --> 01:22:35,567
I don't know.

2338
01:22:35,600 --> 01:22:37,033
MIKE: What do you wanna do?

2339
01:22:37,067 --> 01:22:39,433
Accident. Stupid accident.

2340
01:22:39,467 --> 01:22:40,167
Listen.

2341
01:22:41,267 --> 01:22:43,567
SERVO: I'm late for the Village
People auditions.

2342
01:22:43,600 --> 01:22:45,000
[ Knocks ]

2343
01:22:47,400 --> 01:22:48,767
-It's Johnson.
-Is that you, Biff?

2344
01:22:48,800 --> 01:22:50,433
-JOHNSON: Yeah.
-CROW: Biff Johnson,

2345
01:22:50,467 --> 01:22:51,600
security guard.

2346
01:22:52,600 --> 01:22:53,767
-Hmm?
-Sorry, I'm late, Pete.

2347
01:22:53,800 --> 01:22:54,867
There was an accident.

2348
01:22:56,267 --> 01:22:57,467
Have fun.

2349
01:22:58,467 --> 01:23:00,333
SERVO: Oh, he's hitting them
with a hotdog.

2350
01:23:00,367 --> 01:23:01,600
CROW: Hmm.

2351
01:23:01,633 --> 01:23:02,800
SERVO: All right.

2352
01:23:03,600 --> 01:23:06,267
♪ We hate you, comrade ♪

2353
01:23:08,133 --> 01:23:10,100
SERVO: Let's pose them
so that they're kissing.

2354
01:23:10,133 --> 01:23:11,833
[ Servo and Crow laughs ]

2355
01:23:11,867 --> 01:23:15,300
[ Music playing ]

2356
01:23:15,333 --> 01:23:17,300
SERVO: ♪ Maryanne ♪

2357
01:23:17,333 --> 01:23:20,967
♪ Madame Light, Maryanne ♪

2358
01:23:21,000 --> 01:23:24,300
CROW: Ironically, Marv was about
to get a million dollar raise.

2359
01:23:24,333 --> 01:23:25,633
SERVO: Bet you'd be
pretty impressed,

2360
01:23:25,667 --> 01:23:26,967
if you knew
the shipping clerk here.

2361
01:23:27,000 --> 01:23:27,900
Why, I'm him.

2362
01:23:27,933 --> 01:23:29,633
[ Laughs ]

2363
01:23:29,667 --> 01:23:31,433
[ Tom makes noise ]

2364
01:23:31,467 --> 01:23:33,500
SERVO:
Damn, we need a locksmith.

2365
01:23:33,533 --> 01:23:34,833
Broke off.

2366
01:23:34,867 --> 01:23:36,167
Part of it's still in the lock.

2367
01:23:36,200 --> 01:23:38,167
Come on, it's 7 after,
we haven't got much time.

2368
01:23:40,433 --> 01:23:41,600
This might do it.

2369
01:23:44,000 --> 01:23:45,367
CROW: It wasn't even locked.

2370
01:23:45,400 --> 01:23:48,500
SERVO: Sure increased
the tension, though, huh?

2371
01:23:48,533 --> 01:23:50,033
MIKE: Guys,
we shouldn't be in here,

2372
01:23:50,067 --> 01:23:51,333
the sign said private.

2373
01:23:53,000 --> 01:23:54,100
CROW: A safe?

2374
01:23:54,133 --> 01:23:56,233
I thought you said the money
was in a toaster.

2375
01:23:56,267 --> 01:23:57,367
Well, you're in luck.

2376
01:23:57,400 --> 01:23:58,533
This one's easy.

2377
01:23:59,867 --> 01:24:00,967
It's 11:08.

2378
01:24:01,000 --> 01:24:01,967
Fingers crossed.

2379
01:24:02,000 --> 01:24:03,300
[ Knocks on door ]

2380
01:24:04,333 --> 01:24:06,700
-MRS. FISHER: Mr. Grant.
-SERVO: It's me, Mary.

2381
01:24:06,733 --> 01:24:07,767
MRS. FISHER: Are you there?

2382
01:24:08,800 --> 01:24:11,633
SERVO: I'm wearing my apron
and nothing else.

2383
01:24:11,667 --> 01:24:14,100
CROW: You're not eating beans
in there, are you?

2384
01:24:14,133 --> 01:24:15,167
It's Mrs. Fisher.

2385
01:24:15,200 --> 01:24:17,467
SERVO: I brought
my assortment of nuts.

2386
01:24:19,333 --> 01:24:21,433
CROW: This should be...

2387
01:24:21,467 --> 01:24:24,500
[ Music playing ]

2388
01:24:24,533 --> 01:24:25,433
[ Mrs. Fisher screams]

2389
01:24:25,467 --> 01:24:27,300
SERVO: Oh, my God.
He's a puppeteer.

2390
01:24:27,333 --> 01:24:28,367
CROW: Oh, how horrible.

2391
01:24:28,400 --> 01:24:30,100
MIKE: Many horses far away.

2392
01:24:31,333 --> 01:24:32,500
-SERVO: Ooh.
-CROW: Well, Vince

2393
01:24:32,533 --> 01:24:34,033
has assembled his brain trust.

2394
01:24:34,067 --> 01:24:35,600
[ Tom laughs ]

2395
01:24:36,633 --> 01:24:39,300
MIKE: I have no idea
what I'm doing.

2396
01:24:39,333 --> 01:24:41,600
CROW: Go home, go home.

2397
01:24:43,667 --> 01:24:45,467
MIKE: I have determined
it's a safe.

2398
01:24:46,733 --> 01:24:49,367
CROW: Park in the old canning
lot. What were you thinking?

2399
01:24:49,400 --> 01:24:51,033
-MIKE: Geez.
-CROW: Now turn your head

2400
01:24:51,067 --> 01:24:52,133
and cough.

2401
01:24:53,200 --> 01:24:55,600
SERVO: I have a girlfriend.
Oh.

2402
01:24:57,533 --> 01:25:00,267
MIKE: Guys, I think I'm coming
down with something.

2403
01:25:01,800 --> 01:25:03,833
[ Distant sirens wailing ]

2404
01:25:03,867 --> 01:25:06,067
CROW: Should I have not
called the cops?

2405
01:25:09,000 --> 01:25:10,833
MIKE: Should I tell them or not?

2406
01:25:10,867 --> 01:25:11,767
[ Crow laughs ]

2407
01:25:11,800 --> 01:25:12,900
Got it.

2408
01:25:12,933 --> 01:25:14,033
[ Music playing ]

2409
01:25:14,067 --> 01:25:15,967
-CROW: Oh.
-HARRY: Look at it.

2410
01:25:16,000 --> 01:25:17,633
-SERVO: Ooh.
-HARRY: Million bucks.

2411
01:25:17,667 --> 01:25:19,667
It's beautiful.

2412
01:25:19,700 --> 01:25:21,100
Come on.
We haven't much time.

2413
01:25:21,133 --> 01:25:23,967
SERVO: It's all Wisconsin Dells
Wampum Bucks.

2414
01:25:24,000 --> 01:25:25,167
What is he stealing?

2415
01:25:26,400 --> 01:25:28,967
SERVO: Take it easy, or I won't
have room for my sweater.

2416
01:25:29,000 --> 01:25:30,233
[ Laughs ]

2417
01:25:30,267 --> 01:25:32,433
CROW: Glad you can make
the heist, Mr. Disney.

2418
01:25:32,467 --> 01:25:33,500
SERVO: You shut up.

2419
01:25:33,533 --> 01:25:34,900
CROW: Got a hernia.

2420
01:25:34,933 --> 01:25:38,333
[ Music playing ]

2421
01:25:38,367 --> 01:25:39,367
Come on.

2422
01:25:39,400 --> 01:25:41,000
SERVO: I wanna show you my desk
before we leave.

2423
01:25:44,633 --> 01:25:46,367
SAM: Come on, Harry.

2424
01:25:46,400 --> 01:25:47,400
SERVO: Huh?

2425
01:25:48,867 --> 01:25:51,800
MIKE: Did I tell you we have
honor system candy here?

2426
01:25:53,133 --> 01:25:54,300
SERVO: Oh, ho, ho.

2427
01:25:54,333 --> 01:25:56,433
Oh, ho, ho, ho, ho.

2428
01:25:56,467 --> 01:25:58,167
CROW: Remember when I told you
about that guy

2429
01:25:58,200 --> 01:25:59,233
who doesn't pay for coffee?

2430
01:25:59,267 --> 01:26:00,700
Well, that's his desk
over there.

2431
01:26:00,733 --> 01:26:01,633
[ Tom laughs ]

2432
01:26:01,667 --> 01:26:03,200
MIKE: Unfortunately,
Marv will get caught

2433
01:26:03,233 --> 01:26:06,300
when he turns in his timecard
with these hours on it.

2434
01:26:06,333 --> 01:26:06,900
SERVO: Oops.

2435
01:26:08,067 --> 01:26:11,433
CROW: All of this because
of a strict English teacher.

2436
01:26:11,467 --> 01:26:12,733
[ Tom laughs ]

2437
01:26:13,733 --> 01:26:15,867
MARV: Okay.
That's far enough.

2438
01:26:15,900 --> 01:26:16,867
-SERVO: Oh, hi, Vince.
-Vince.

2439
01:26:16,900 --> 01:26:18,433
Give me that case
right now.

2440
01:26:18,467 --> 01:26:20,167
Vince, look, the cops
will be here any minute.

2441
01:26:20,200 --> 01:26:21,100
You can have some.

2442
01:26:21,133 --> 01:26:22,433
Shut up and give me
that money!

2443
01:26:22,467 --> 01:26:24,633
MIKE:
I'll write your paper, Vince.

2444
01:26:24,667 --> 01:26:27,667
[ Music playing ]

2445
01:26:29,667 --> 01:26:31,100
CROW: Damn, I missed Marv.

2446
01:26:31,133 --> 01:26:32,033
Are you crazy, Vince?

2447
01:26:32,067 --> 01:26:33,633
You didn't have to do that.

2448
01:26:33,667 --> 01:26:35,700
Come on, let's go, Larry.

2449
01:26:35,733 --> 01:26:37,733
SERVO: There goes the town's
only liquor store.

2450
01:26:38,800 --> 01:26:40,633
He's the last
of the great gentlemen.

2451
01:26:40,667 --> 01:26:43,833
MIKE: That's who we should've
gotten for the heist.

2452
01:26:43,867 --> 01:26:45,533
CROW: And seconds
into Vince's plan

2453
01:26:45,567 --> 01:26:47,833
-and it all goes wrong.
-...even have a gun.

2454
01:26:49,833 --> 01:26:52,367
-Vince.
-SERVO: And I helped.

2455
01:26:52,400 --> 01:26:55,200
Vince, come on.
Don't just stand there.

2456
01:26:57,067 --> 01:26:58,833
-You made me kill him.
-Come on.

2457
01:26:58,867 --> 01:27:00,400
Come on!

2458
01:27:02,267 --> 01:27:04,567
-Vince.
-SERVO: This is cashmere.

2459
01:27:04,600 --> 01:27:06,100
No, Vince.

2460
01:27:06,133 --> 01:27:08,400
SERVO:
Pepperidge Farm remembers...

2461
01:27:09,433 --> 01:27:11,100
[ Gunshots ]

2462
01:27:11,133 --> 01:27:13,567
CROW: I think this is about
more than the heist.

2463
01:27:13,600 --> 01:27:15,067
MIKE: Oh, geez.

2464
01:27:17,067 --> 01:27:18,367
There they are.

2465
01:27:18,400 --> 01:27:19,633
[ Gunshot ]

2466
01:27:19,667 --> 01:27:21,333
CROW: Hey, Baryshnikov!

2467
01:27:25,867 --> 01:27:26,933
Huh, liquid assets.

2468
01:27:26,967 --> 01:27:29,033
Million bucks.

2469
01:27:29,067 --> 01:27:30,433
-SERVO: He's juicy.
-MAN: Forget the money.

2470
01:27:30,467 --> 01:27:32,300
Let's get out of here.

2471
01:27:32,333 --> 01:27:36,167
I am loaded down
with snow, remember?

2472
01:27:36,200 --> 01:27:37,300
[ Distant siren wailing ]

2473
01:27:37,333 --> 01:27:40,867
SERVO: Ah, Ricky.

2474
01:27:41,867 --> 01:27:43,567
Don't move.

2475
01:27:43,600 --> 01:27:45,733
Now you have the right
to remain silent.

2476
01:27:45,767 --> 01:27:46,600
[ Gunshot ]

2477
01:27:46,633 --> 01:27:47,833
-Right there.
-Anything you say can

2478
01:27:47,867 --> 01:27:48,967
and will be used against you.

2479
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:52,300
MIKE: Oh, no need to launder
the money then.

2480
01:27:52,333 --> 01:27:53,733
CROW: Would you stop?

2481
01:27:55,733 --> 01:27:56,833
Why?

2482
01:27:58,733 --> 01:28:00,967
CROW: I got punched
right in the store. Oh.

2483
01:28:01,000 --> 01:28:04,867
Oh, forgive me, I'm sorry, Pop.

2484
01:28:05,867 --> 01:28:07,700
Forgive me, Pop.

2485
01:28:07,733 --> 01:28:09,767
SERVO: I could really go
for a pop.

2486
01:28:09,800 --> 01:28:12,800
[ Sirens wailing ]

2487
01:28:14,133 --> 01:28:16,133
SERVO: Reverse-angle cops.

2488
01:28:19,200 --> 01:28:21,333
Oh, how'd the heist go?

2489
01:28:22,333 --> 01:28:24,633
Oh, geez, what a mess.

2490
01:28:24,667 --> 01:28:27,167
I just came from a scene
where some unemployed bean-eater

2491
01:28:27,200 --> 01:28:29,200
was swinging from the ceiling.

2492
01:28:30,200 --> 01:28:32,567
[ Mike imitates music ]

2493
01:28:32,600 --> 01:28:34,833
CROW: Should we just leave
the dead guys there?

2494
01:28:34,867 --> 01:28:36,300
SERVO: The crows will get them.

2495
01:28:36,333 --> 01:28:37,233
CROW: Yeah.

2496
01:28:37,267 --> 01:28:38,167
MIKE: Gross.

2497
01:28:38,200 --> 01:28:40,200
[ Servo makes noises ]

2498
01:28:41,533 --> 01:28:43,367
CROW: This is the PTA,
reminding you

2499
01:28:43,400 --> 01:28:45,767
to always do your homework.

2500
01:28:45,800 --> 01:28:47,833
SERVO: You know, in light
of this, cheating on a paper

2501
01:28:47,867 --> 01:28:49,767
wasn't that big a deal.

2502
01:28:49,800 --> 01:28:51,900
Coming up next on Nick at Nite.

2503
01:28:51,933 --> 01:28:53,300
One of the original
black and white

2504
01:28:53,333 --> 01:28:55,767
I Dream of Jeannie episodes.

2505
01:28:55,800 --> 01:28:58,900
Then F-Troop,
